          },
          {
            "name" : "Description",
            "value" : "Apical-to-basolateral transport of pesticides across a Caco-2 cell monolayer cultured on Transwell inserts (GBO ThinCert, 0.4 µm pore, 0.336 cm² growth area, 24-well) with a stable TEER. Cells were exposed apically to pesticide dissolved in HBSS (with Ca²⁺/Mg²⁺; max 0.1% DMSO); 50–100 µL samples were collected from the apical and basolateral compartments at 0.01, 0.5, 1, 2 and 5 h (or 0.01, 2 and 4 h) and the insert was extracted at the final time point, then diluted 1:1 in LC-MS/MS-grade methanol (1:2 in cyclohexane for endosulfan). Pesticide concentrations were quantified by LC-MS/MS and used to derive apparent permeability (Papp) / fraction absorbed."
          },
          {
            "name" : "Replicates",
            "value" : "3"
          },
          {
            "name" : "Technical replicates",
            "value" : "2"
